.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the CLI of two things that share one binary: the
.Cm juggler daemon
llama-server control plane, and the agent substrate of FDR 0019
.Pq Pa docs/features/0019-juggler-agent-substrate.md ,
the headless, tool-using agents launched by
.Cm spawn .
.Pp
The instance-management and registry subcommands
.Pq Cm start , stop , status , list , models , model , prompt , mcp
dial the control socket, issue JSON-RPC calls and pretty-print the
result; a
.Cm juggler daemon
must be running before they can complete.
The
.Sx programs.juggler
home-manager module starts and supervises it; users without
home-manager must invoke
.Cm juggler daemon
themselves.
If the control socket is missing or refuses connections,
.Nm
prints a one-paragraph hint pointing at the home-manager module before
returning a non-zero exit code.
.Pp
The agent-substrate subcommands
.Pq Cm run , spawn , exit-wake , resolve , job-ledger , handles , decide
do not need the daemon for the common case.
.Cm run , decide
and
.Cm spawn
resolve a
.Em remote
registry entry
.Pq see Xr juggler 7 Sx MODEL REGISTRY
straight from the models file
.Pq Ev JUGGLER_MODELS_PATH ;
only a
.Em local
GGUF model sends them to the daemon, which owns the llama-server
process.
.Cm exit-wake , resolve , job-ledger
and
.Cm handles
never dial the daemon.
Like
.Cm download ,
none of these is a JSON-RPC call.
They consume
.Xr ringmaster 1
(jobs; protocol version 2 or later, for
.Ql aborted ,
.Ql cancel-requested ,
.Ic cancel
and
.Ic wait Fl -on-cancel ) ,
.Xr troupe 1
(identity and the run's MUC; a version with
.Ic mint Fl -password-file )
and
.Xr systemd-run 1
(one transient unit per agent) as external binaries; see
.Sx ENVIRONMENT .
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm daemon Op Fl -socket Ar path Op Fl -llama-server Ar path
Run the llama-server control-plane daemon that the instance-management
and registry subcommands dial.
Binds the control socket
.Pq Pa ~/.local/state/juggler/control.sock ,
overridable with
.Fl -socket ,
and exec's the build-time
.Pa llama-server
binary,
overridable with
.Fl -llama-server .
This is the server end of the control plane.
The job platform it once shared a binary with was extracted into the
standalone
.Ql code.linenisgreat.com/ringmaster
module.
Normally started by the
.Sx programs.juggler
home-manager module rather than by hand.
.It Cm start Ar model Op Fl -alias Ar name Op Fl -bind Ar addr Op Cm -- Ar passthrough\&...
Spawn a new llama-server child via the control-plane daemon.
The required positional
.Ar model
is the bare name of a
.Pa .gguf
file under
.Pa ~/.local/share/juggler/models
.Pq or an absolute path .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -alias Ar name
Registry key for the new instance.
Defaults to
.Ar model
when omitted.
Both
.Sq Fl -alias Ar name
and
.Sq Fl -alias Ns = Ns Ar name
parse.
.It Fl -bind Ar addr
Bind address for the spawned llama-server.
Defaults to
.Sq 127.0.0.1 .
Set to
.Sq 0.0.0.0
to bind every interface (e.g. for tailscale-reachable instances) or
to a specific tailnet IP.
.It Cm -- Ar passthrough\&...
Any args after
.Cm --
are forwarded to llama-server verbatim via the JSON-RPC
.Sq Args
field, e.g.
.Sq Fl -ctx-size 32768 .
.El
On success prints
.Sq juggler: started <alias> at <bind>:<port> (pid <pid>) .
.It Cm stop Ar alias
Send SIGTERM to the named instance's process group via juggler, wait
up to five seconds, then SIGKILL.
Removes the entry from the registry.
.It Cm status Op Ar alias
Without
.Ar alias :
print a tabwriter table of every registered instance, or
.Sq juggler: no instances running
when the registry is empty.
With
.Ar alias :
print one-key-per-line detail for the named instance, including
RFC 3339 start time and a humanized uptime.
.It Cm list
Same column set as
.Cm status ,
but silent on empty
.Pq exit code 0, zero bytes of output .
Use for scripted consumption; use
.Cm status
for interactive sessions.
.It Cm models
Print the names of every
.Pa *.gguf
file under
.Pa ~/.local/share/juggler/models ,
one per line.
Backed by juggler's
.Cm ListAvailableModels
RPC so the same file is seen by both juggler and clown.
.It Cm model Cm list , Cm add Ar name , No or Cm remove Ar name
Manage the unified model registry
.Pq local and remote; see Xr juggler 7 Sx MODEL REGISTRY .
These dial the daemon, which owns the models file; the substrate verbs
read the same file directly.
Deliberately a separate command from
.Cm models
.Pq plural, above, which stays local-GGUF-only, one name per line
for back-compat with existing scripts.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm list
Print a
.Sq NAME KIND STYLE
table of every local and remote model, backed by juggler's
.Cm ListModels
RPC.
.Sy KIND
is
.Sq local
or
.Sq remote ;
.Sy STYLE
is populated only for remote entries.
.It Cm add Ar name Fl -style Ar style Fl -url Ar url Bro Fl -token Ar token | Fl -token-file Ar path Brc Op Fl -model Ar id
Register
.Pq or replace
a remote model in the registry via the
.Cm AddRemoteModel
RPC.
.Ar style
is
.Sq anthropic ,
.Sq openai-compat
or
.Sq decisions ;
any other value is rejected before any RPC call is attempted.
.Sq decisions
entries are consumed only by
.Cm decide
and are rejected by
.Cm prompt
and the agent loop.
.Fl -style
and
.Fl -url
are required, and exactly one of
.Fl -token
and
.Fl -token-file
must be given.
.Fl -token
is a literal secret or a
.Ql ${VAR}
reference expanded when the entry is resolved.
.Fl -token-file
names a file
.Po
.Ql ~/
and
.Ql $VAR
expanded
.Pc
whose trimmed contents are the token: the by-reference credential a
hardened headless host uses instead of a secret in the models file.
.Fl -model
is the upstream model id sent to the provider; the registry
.Ar name
is then a stable alias for it
.Pq default: Ar name No itself .
Both
.Sq Fl -style Ar value
and
.Sq Fl -style Ns = Ns Ar value
forms parse, matching
.Cm start Ns 's
.Fl -alias
convention.
On success prints
.Sq juggler: registered remote model "<name>" .
.It Cm remove Ar name
Delete the named remote model via the
.Cm RemoveRemoteModel
RPC.
Errors if
.Ar name
is not a registered remote model.
On success prints
.Sq juggler: removed remote model "<name>" .
.El
.It Cm prompt Ar model Op Ar prompt-text\&... Op Fl -max-tokens Ar n
Resolve
.Ar model
through the
.Cm ResolveModel
RPC
.Pq the same resolution juggler-backed profiles use: remote registry first, then an already-running local instance, then a freshly started local GGUF instance
and send it a single prompt, printing the reply to stdout and exiting.
A
.Sq Cm claude Fl p
-shaped direct smoke path: nothing but juggler's own resolution and
HTTP-call machinery is exercised, no clown or claude-code in the loop.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar prompt-text\&...
Remaining positional arguments are joined with a single space to form
the prompt.
When omitted entirely, the prompt is read from stdin instead
.Pq trailing newline trimmed .
.It Fl -max-tokens Ar n
Maximum tokens to generate.
Defaults to 256.
Both
.Sq Fl -max-tokens Ar n
and
.Sq Fl -max-tokens Ns = Ns Ar n
forms parse.
.El
A single 120-second budget covers both the
.Cm ResolveModel
call
.Pq which may block starting a local instance
and the completion request itself.
A local result always resolves to an Anthropic-Messages-shaped endpoint
.Pq Sq POST Pa /v1/messages ,
.Sq anthropic-version: 2023-06-01
and authenticates with
.Sq x-api-key: dummy .
A remote result's registered style picks the protocol:
.Sq anthropic
sends the same Anthropic-Messages-shaped request, authenticating with
.Sq x-api-key
set to the registered token;
.Sq openai-compat
sends an OpenAI Chat Completions-shaped request
.Pq Sq POST Pa /chat/completions ,
authenticating with
.Sq Authorization: Bearer <token> .
Any other style errors cleanly before any HTTP call is attempted.
.It Cm download Ar name Op Fl Fl url Ar url Op Fl Fl sha256 Ar hex Op Fl Fl size Ar bytes
Fetch a model with a bubbletea progress UI.
When
.Ar name
matches an entry in the baked-in registry and
.Fl Fl url
is omitted, the URL, expected SHA-256, and size are taken from the
registry (the common case).
When
.Fl Fl url
is provided, an ad-hoc download is performed from the given URL;
.Fl Fl sha256
is recommended but optional (a warning is printed when omitted), and
.Fl Fl size
populates the progress-bar denominator (otherwise the bar runs
indeterminate).
When both a registry hit and
.Fl Fl url
are present, the URL overrides the registry entry.
Does NOT go through juggler; uses
.Sy jugglermodels.Download
directly because juggler's
.Cm DownloadModel
RPC is synchronous (no progress events on the wire) and not the
right surface for a terminal-attached invocation.
The downloaded file lands in
.Pa ~/.local/share/juggler/models
where every other subcommand can see it.
.It Cm mcp
Run a stdio MCP server exposing a single tool,
.Sq juggler-prompt ,
taking
.Sq model ,
.Sq task ,
and an optional
.Sq max_tokens
and returning the model's text reply.
Normally spawned by Claude Code itself as the
.Cm clown-builtin-juggler
plugin's
.Sq stdioServers
entry
.Pq Sq juggler mcp ,
not invoked directly by a human.
Each
.Sq tools/call
resolves
.Ar model
and sends
.Ar task
through the same
.Cm ResolveModel
resolution and HTTP dispatch machinery
.Cm prompt
uses, under the same 120-second budget.
.Ar max_tokens
defaults to 1024 when omitted, higher than
.Cm prompt Ns 's
256-token CLI default since this tool is for real delegated work
rather than a smoke test.
This tool makes real, and for remote models potentially paid,
third-party API calls, so the plugin ships no auto-allow hook for it;
every call defers to Claude Code's own permission prompt
.Pq see Pa docs/plans/2026-07-11-juggler-subagent-tool-design.md for the reasoning .
.It Cm run Fl -brief Ar file Op Fl -job Ar id Op Fl -brief-stanza Ar id Op Fl -moxy Ar path | Fl -moxy-url Ar url
The agent.
Reads its brief
.Pq TOML; Ar file No or Sq Fl No for stdin ,
resolves the brief's model
.Pq daemon-free for a remote registry entry ,
launches one moxy instance from the brief's inline moxyfile and drives
the model's tool-use loop through it until the model ends its turn,
calls
.Ql cannot_complete ,
or hits the brief's step cap or wall clock.
Every tool call is recorded in the ledger; at the end the brief's
evaluator
.Pq a jq program
collapses the ledger into the verdict, which becomes the ringmaster
job's terminal record.
It is a ringmaster
.Em producer ,
not a ringmaster-spawned process.
Normally started by
.Cm spawn
as a transient unit rather than by hand.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -job Ar id
Adopt this pre-started ringmaster job
.Pq Cm spawn No passes it
instead of starting one.
.It Fl -brief-stanza Ar id
The brief's stanza id in the run's room; the first recorded turn's
provenance parent.
.It Fl -moxy Ar path
The moxy binary launched
.Pq default Ev JUGGLER_MOXY_BIN ,
.It Fl -moxy-url Ar url
Use this already-running MCP upstream instead of launching moxy
.Pq default Ev JUGGLER_MOXY_URL ; No for tests .
.It Fl -ringmaster Ar path , Fl -troupe Ar path
The consumed binaries; see
.Sx ENVIRONMENT .
.El
The principal is the brief's
.Ql principal ;
.Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID ,
when set, must equal it.
That variable and every
.Ev TROUPE_XMPP_*
and
.Ev TROUPE_MINT_*
variable are stripped from the environment handed to moxy and its tool
servers.
SIGTERM or SIGINT
.Pq Ql systemctl stop ,
or a holder's
.Ql ringmaster cancel ,
terminalizes the job
.Ql aborted .
The moxyfile is written under
.Pa agents/<principal>/
in the state directory.
Prints one JSON object
.Sy {"job","state","message","ledger"}
and exits with the state: 0
.Ql succeeded ,
2
.Ql failed ,
3
.Ql aborted ,
4
.Ql interrupted ;
1 is a usage or identity error with no job written.
.It Cm spawn Fl -new-run Op Fl -run-key Ar key Fl -input Ar file Op Fl -issuer Ar principal Fl -room Ar jid | Fl -room-domain Ar domain Fl -operator-jid Ar jid
The issuer's entry for a new tree: start a
.Em run .
Mints the run's root principal
.Pq Ql troupe mint Fl -session-key Fl -password-file ;
the credential is kept by reference, in one password file per identity
under the run's state directory, never in argv or stdout ,
posts the run's input
.Pq Ar file No or Sq Fl No for stdin ; JSON is embedded as is, anything else as a string
as the room's root stanza, and starts a run-level ringmaster job on the
issuer's channel with the issuer as its first handle holder.
Every later step of the run executes as the run root.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -run-key Ar key
Caller-supplied idempotency key
.Pq derived from the recording .
An existing run with that key is returned unchanged with
.Ql "existing": true
and nothing is created.
Without it a fresh key is minted.
The root principal is the UUIDv5 of the key under juggler's fixed
namespace, so the key must never be reused for a different run.
.It Fl -issuer Ar principal
The issuer
.Pq default Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID .
.It Fl -room Ar jid
An existing, already-configured run MUC.
It stays its owner's: children are not affiliated into it and the root
does not step down from it.
.It Fl -room-domain Ar domain
Create the run's MUC
.Ar run-key Ns @ Ns Ar domain
.Pq run key lowercased
as the run root:
.Ql troupe muc create Fl -room Ar room Fl -owner Ar operator-jid ,
with the root's
.Ev TROUPE_XMPP_USER
and
.Ev TROUPE_XMPP_PASSWORD_FILE .
The root owns the room it creates; the operator is its second owner,
so the root can step down at
.Cm resolve
.Pq the last owner cannot .
Each later
.Cm spawn Fl -brief
affiliates its child as a member before the unit starts.
A failure after the room exists leaves it
.Pq rooms are persistent; the retention sweep removes them ;
a retry with the same
.Fl -run-key
re-creates it idempotently as the same root.
.It Fl -operator-jid Ar jid
The operator's bare JID
.Pq default Ev JUGGLER_OPERATOR_JID ;
required with
.Fl -room-domain .
.El
Prints
.Sy {"run_key","root_principal","root_credential_ref","root_jid","room","root_stanza","run_job","operator_jid","existing","resumed","resolved","torn_down"}
.Pq Ql operator_jid No and Ql resumed No only when set .
.Ql existing
is true exactly for a complete run found under the key;
.Ql resumed
is true when this call finished a
.Ql pending
run
.Pq Ql existing No is false then .
.Ql root_stanza
is the run-input stanza id that
.Cm decide Fl -parent
takes; on an existing run,
.Ql resolved
and
.Ql torn_down
tell a redelivery how far the first delivery got, so one that crashed
before
.Cm resolve
can be finished instead of dropped.
Exit status 0, or 1 on a usage or launch failure.
A failure after the root's mint keeps the root
.Pq its account and password file
and any created room, withdraws a posted run input, fails a started run
job and saves the run as
.Ql pending ;
the same command with the same
.Fl -run-key
resumes it, re-minting the same root.
Such a failure prints one line
.Sy {"run_key","pending":true,"root_principal","room"}
on stdout
.Pq the cause on stderr ;
a failure of the mint itself saves nothing and prints nothing on stdout.
A pending run takes no subagents, and
.Cm decide Fl -run-key
refuses it before any model call.
One that is never retried leaves the root and room for the retention
sweep.
.It Cm spawn Fl -brief Ar template Op Fl -task Ar file Op Fl -run-key Ar key Op Fl -wait Op Fl -timeout Ar dur Op Fl -stop-grace Ar dur Op Fl -moxy-url Ar url Op Fl -juggler Ar path Op Fl -user
Launch one subagent into a run.
.Ar template
is a brief
.Pq TOML; Ar file No or Sq Fl No for stdin
without
.Ql principal ,
.Ql parent ,
.Ql room
and
.Ql task ;
the spawner fills them
.Pq a minted child key, the run root, the run's room, the task content ,
then validates the filled brief strictly.
.Ql model ,
.Ql system ,
.Ql tools ,
.Ql evaluator
and
.Ql limits
must be in the template; its
.Ql model
is the author's choice of registry entry, which the spawner's models
file must define for the agent to start.
The run is the one named by
.Fl -run-key ,
else the one that owns the template's
.Ql room ,
else the one whose root principal is
.Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID
.Pq the glue runs as the run root .
A resolved run refuses new subagents.
.Pp
The child's principal and JID are minted; in a room the run created,
the root then admits the JID
.Pq Ql troupe muc affiliate Fl -room Ar room Fl -affiliation No member Fl -jid Ar child ,
undone with
.Ql none
if the spawn fails; the brief is staged under the
run's
.Pa children/
directory and dropped into the room as a stanza, the child's job is
started on the run root's channel with the root as first holder, and
the child runs as a systemd transient unit
.Pq Ql juggler-agent-<principal> ,
started with
.Xr systemd-run 1
.Fl -collect
.Fl -property=Type=exec
.Fl -property=Delegate=yes
.Fl -property=RuntimeMaxSec=<wall clock + stop grace>
and
.Fl -property=ExecStopPost=<juggler> exit-wake --job <job> --target <run root> ,
which makes the unit's post-stop hook the sole exit-wake emitter.
If any step fails, everything created so far is undone and the room is
left with a withdrawal stanza, never an orphan brief.
A subagent spawned with the same brief and task into the same run is
idempotent: it returns the existing child and starts no second unit.
.Pp
The unit's environment is exactly: the child's identity
.Pq Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID No = the child's principal, and Ev TROUPE_XMPP_USER , TROUPE_XMPP_PASSWORD_FILE , TROUPE_XMPP_DOMAIN No of its minted account ,
the brief's own
.Ql [env]
table
.Pq keys CLOWN_SESSION_ID , TROUPE_XMPP_* , TROUPE_MINT_* No and JUGGLER_* are reserved and rejected ,
.Ev JUGGLER_MOXY_URL
when
.Fl -moxy-url
or the variable is set, and these variables of the spawner's when set:
.Ev XDG_STATE_HOME ,
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR ,
.Ev JUGGLER_MODELS_PATH ,
.Ev JUGGLER_RINGMASTER_BIN ,
.Ev JUGGLER_TROUPE_BIN ,
.Ev JUGGLER_MOXY_BIN ,
.Ev TROUPE_TRANSPORT ,
.Ev TROUPE_XMPP_HOST ,
.Ev TROUPE_XMPP_PORT
and
.Ev TROUPE_XMPP_INSECURE .
The spawner's own
.Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID ,
.Ev TROUPE_XMPP_*
identity and
.Ev TROUPE_MINT_*
minter credential are stripped from the environment of the
.Xr systemd-run 1
client process, so they never reach a unit.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -task Ar file
The brief's task text
.Pq Sq Fl No for stdin ;
default: the template's own.
.Fl -brief
and
.Fl -task
cannot both read stdin.
.It Fl -wait
Block until the subagent's job terminalizes and print its verdict,
exiting with its state; see below.
Without it the launch object
.Sy {"jid","job","room"}
is printed immediately and the exit status is 0.
.It Fl -timeout Ar dur
Bound for
.Fl -wait
.Pq default: the brief's wall clock plus twice the stop grace ,
the point past which the unit's backstop has written the terminal.
At the timeout the child job is asked to cancel
.Pq Ql ringmaster cancel
and given
.Fl -stop-grace
to terminalize, so a caller that falls back never races a late agent.
Only a wait that really used up its timeout cancels the job.
.It Fl -stop-grace Ar dur
Default 30s.
Added to the brief's wall clock for the unit's
.Ql RuntimeMaxSec
backstop, and the time a cancelled job is given to terminalize.
.It Fl -juggler Ar path
The juggler binary the unit runs
.Pq default: this executable .
.It Fl -user
Start the unit under the user service manager
.Pq Ql systemd-run Fl -user ;
for a hardened service user that cannot ask the system manager for a
transient unit.
.It Fl -ringmaster Ar path , Fl -troupe Ar path , Fl -systemd-run Ar path
The consumed binaries; see
.Sx ENVIRONMENT .
.El
.Pp
With
.Fl -wait ,
prints
.Sy {"jid","job","room","state","reason","message","ledger","artifacts":[{"tool","kind","uris"}],"cannot_complete":null|{"reason"}} .
.Ql state
is the ringmaster state
.Pq or Ql running ,
.Ql reason
the FDR 0032 D6 exit reason
.Pq Ql normal , failed , shutdown , crash , killed ,
.Ql ledger
the path of the result spool, and
.Ql artifacts
the URIs the successful tool calls returned.
Exit status:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact -offset indent
.It 0
launched, or
.Ql succeeded
.It 1
usage or launch failure
.It 2
.Ql failed
.It 3
.Ql aborted
.Pq including a cancel at the timeout that terminalized within the stop grace
.It 4
.Ql interrupted
.It 5
the timeout elapsed, a cancel was requested, and the job was still not
terminal after the stop grace
.Pq Ql state No is Ql running
.El
.It Cm exit-wake Fl -job Ar id Fl -target Ar principal Op Fl -run-ledger Ar path Op Fl -from Ar principal
The agent unit's
.Ql ExecStopPost
hook and the sole exit-wake emitter.
systemd runs it as a fresh process after the main process is gone, on
every ending, and tells it how the unit ended in
.Ev SERVICE_RESULT ,
.Ev EXIT_CODE
and
.Ev EXIT_STATUS .
.Fl -job
is the agent's job and
.Fl -target
the channel that holds it
.Pq the agent's parent principal .
When the main process left no terminal record the hook writes one:
.Bl -tag -width "exit-code, core-dump, oom-kill" -offset indent
.It Ql success
the terminal
.Cm run
already wrote
.Pq Ql succeeded No or Ql failed
is relayed, reason
.Ql normal
or
.Ql failed ;
if it wrote none, the hook writes
.Ql interrupted
.Pq crash
.It Ql timeout
.Ql failed ,
reason
.Ql failed
.Pq the unit's Ql RuntimeMaxSec No backstop expired
.It Ql signal
.Ql interrupted ,
reason
.Ql killed
.It Ql exit-code , core-dump , oom-kill
.Ql interrupted ,
reason
.Ql crash
.El
.Pp
It then sends ONE wake
.Pq Ql troupe message
to every accepted holder on the job's journal, carrying
.Ql exit <job> <state> reason=<reason> [<message>]
and the terminal's
.Ql result_ref .
A pending or released handle is sent nothing.
The hook is idempotent: it never writes a second terminal record, and a
marker file
.Pa exit-wakes/<job>
in the state directory, written once every send succeeded, stops a rerun
from waking again.
.Fl -run-ledger
is the
.Ql result_ref
to attach when the hook writes the terminal itself;
.Fl -from
the exiting principal
.Pq default Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID .
Prints
.Sy {"job","state","reason","message","wrote_terminal","woken","already_woken"} ;
exit status 0, or 1 when a record or wake could not be written.
.It Cm resolve Ar run-job Fl -state Ar succeeded|failed Fl -reason Ar text Op Fl -fallback-artifacts Ar json Op Fl -stop-grace Ar dur Op Fl -result-line Ar text Fl -canary-room Ar jid Op Fl -keep-accounts
The run's last call, always.
With
.Fl -result-line
and
.Fl -canary-room
.Pq given together; the line must be one line ,
its first act is to post the line into the canary room as the run root
.Pq Ql troupe muc send Fl -source No juggler-resolve ,
before the root's account is torn down; the post is a
.Ql canary
note in the run ledger, and a failed post changes nothing else.
It then cancels every child job of the run that is not yet terminal and
waits up to
.Fl -stop-grace
.Pq default 30s
for each, so a later account teardown never deletes an account under a
running agent; each one it had to stop is a
.Ql subagent_stop
entry
.Pq Ql stopped_by_resolve ,
ok exactly when the job terminalized within the grace
.Pq a child whose journal cannot be read is recorded as not ok, never fatal .
Then appends a
.Ql fallback
entry to the run ledger, writes the ledger to the run job's result spool,
writes the run job's terminal record
.Pq Ar state , with Ar text No as its message
and sends the run's exit wake to the run job's holders
.Pq the issuer .
.Fl -state
is
.Ql succeeded ,
or
.Ql failed
when the fallback ran; the fallback is expected to run exactly when the
run resolves
.Ql failed .
.Fl -fallback-artifacts
is the fallback's own outcome as a JSON array of
.Sy {"tool","kind","uris"} :
its entry is ok when it did not need to run, or ran and produced at
least one URI.
.Pp
Last, unless
.Fl -keep-accounts ,
it tears the run's accounts down.
For each child whose job is terminal: in a room the run created,
.Ql troupe muc affiliate Fl -affiliation No none Fl -jid Ar child
as the root
.Pq best effort ;
then
.Ql troupe mint-revoke Fl -session-key Ar child Fl -password-file Ar file ;
then the password file is deleted.
Then, once no child account remains, the root sets its own affiliation
to
.Ql none
.Pq only in a room the run created with an operator owner; otherwise skipped and noted ,
revokes itself and deletes its file.
A SASL login refusal at revoke means the account is already gone
.Pq troupe cannot tell it from a wrong password
and the file is deleted anyway: exit 1 with the refusal right after
.Ql xmpp: negotiate:
on stderr
.Po Prosody's
.Dq Unable to authorize you with the authentication credentials ,
or
.Ql not-authorized
.Pc ,
or
.Ql sasl: not-authorized .
Any other revoke failure, a TLS or stream failure during negotiation
included, keeps the account and its file.
A child still running after the grace keeps its account
.Pq Dq still running ,
and the root keeps its own while any child account remains.
Each account handled is a
.Sy {"tool":"teardown","kind":"account","ok","principal","jid","reason"}
run-ledger entry; the run is
.Ql torn_down
once every account is gone.
.Pp
Resolving an already-resolved run rewrites nothing, posts no canary
line and sends no wake: it only performs a teardown still pending
.Pq accounts already gone are skipped ,
prints the stored verdict with a notice on stderr, and exits 0.
A retried partial resolve
.Pq one that failed after the canary post, e.g. on the exit wake
posts no second canary line either: the post is recorded in
.Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/juggler/runs/<run-key>/canary-posted
and in the run ledger the moment it succeeds.
A
.Cm spawn Fl -brief
racing
.Cm resolve
holds the run lock through its launch, so it is either refused or seen by
the teardown.
Prints
.Sy {"run_key","run_job","state","reason","ledger","woken","already_resolved","canary","torn_down","teardown"} .
.Ql canary
is present when
.Fl -canary-room
was given:
.Sy {"room","posted","stanza"} ,
with
.Ql posted
true also when an earlier attempt posted the line
.Pq Ql stanza No is then that post's id .
.Ql teardown
is this call's teardown entries; it is absent when the call handled no
account
.Pq none was kept by an earlier call, or Fl -keep-accounts .
.Pp
The teardown needs the minter credential:
.Ql troupe mint-revoke
takes its privilege-free self-removal path only when a minter credential
is named, and
.Nm
hands troupe its own environment.
.Cm resolve
therefore requires
.Ev TROUPE_MINT_PASSWORD_FILE
.Pq and Ev TROUPE_MINT_USER ;
without
.Fl -keep-accounts
it exits 1 when
.Ev TROUPE_MINT_PASSWORD_FILE
is unset, before the canary post and before stopping any child.
.It Cm job-ledger Ar job Op Fl -target Ar principal
Print a job's ledger: a run job's run ledger, or an agent job's result
spool
.Pq Ql ringmaster spool-path ,
for a caller that did not
.Fl -wait .
.Fl -target
names the channel holding a job juggler's state directory does not know.
Exit status 1 for an unknown job or an empty spool.
.It Cm handles Ar job Op Fl -target Ar principal
Print a job's handle table as a JSON array of
.Sy {"holder","rights","status","granted_by","granted_at"} :
a holder is a principal string, rights a comma-separated list
.Pq default Ql observe,close ,
status
.Ql pending
.Pq confers nothing, and no exit wake, until first use ,
.Ql accepted
or
.Ql released .
Read-only: this version has no grant, accept or release verb.
.It Cm decide Fl -model Ar name Fl -room Ar jid Fl -parent Ar stanza-id Op Fl -min-confidence Ar n Op Fl -question Ar id Op Fl -run-key Ar key
The router.
A synchronous verb, not an agent: one request to an OpenRouter
Decisions-API-style model
.Pq Ql POST /api/alpha/decisions ,
with no loop and no ringmaster job of its own.
Reads the Decisions request minus
.Ql model
and authentication from stdin,
.Sy {"state":\&...,"questions":{\&...}} ,
resolves
.Fl -model
from the registry
.Pq a remote entry with style Ql decisions ; No daemon-free ,
sends the request with the entry's upstream model id and token, applies
the confidence threshold, posts ONE
.Em decision stanza
into
.Fl -room
as the ambient
.Ev TROUPE_XMPP_*
identity
.Pq source Ql juggler-decide ,
whose provenance parent is
.Fl -parent
.Pq the recording's stanza id ,
and prints the answers.
The stanza carries the model, a digest of
.Ql state ,
the questions, the full answers, the threshold and its verdict, and
usage; it is posted for every outcome, including a failed attempt.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -min-confidence Ar n
The usable threshold in [0,1], inclusive
.Pq default 0.5 .
The API's
.Ql confidence
is the MARGIN over the runner-up, not the winning probability
.Pq 0.63 against 0.37 is 0.26 ,
so with two options 0.5 means roughly 0.75 or better; the stanza and
the ledger entry also carry the chosen option's probability.
It is used verbatim, never recomputed.
.It Fl -question Ar id
The question to gate on; required when the request has several.
Only
.Ql choice
questions are gated.
.It Fl -run-key Ar key
Record the outcome as a
.Ql route
entry
.Pq tool, kind Ql route ; ok exactly when usable
in this run's ledger
.Pq see Cm spawn Fl -new-run ,
so the glue never writes ledger entries itself.
The run must exist and be unresolved; checked before any call.
.It Fl -troupe Ar path
The troupe binary; see
.Sx ENVIRONMENT .
.El
Exit status:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact -offset indent
.It 0
a usable choice
.Pq confidence at or above the threshold ,
stanza posted
.It 4
a valid choice below the threshold; stdout and the stanza carry the
choice and its confidence
.It 2
no choice: an HTTP failure, an unparseable response, or a
.Ql choice
that is not one of the question's
.Ql criteria ;
stdout carries
.Sy {"reason","http_status","raw"}
.It 3
decided, but the room post failed
.Pq the provenance chain is broken ;
stdout and the route entry are still produced
.It 1
usage or configuration error before any call
.El
.Pp
Every non-zero exit is a failed
.Ql route
entry in the run ledger, and the run resolves to the fallback.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev JUGGLER_SOCKET
Override the control socket path
.Pq Pa ~/.local/state/juggler/control.sock No by default .
Read by both
.Nm
and the
.Cm juggler daemon ,
so setting it consistently is sufficient.
.It Ev JUGGLER_MODELS_PATH
The remote-model registry file
.Pq Pa ~/.local/share/juggler/models.toml No by default .
Read by the daemon and, directly, by
.Cm run , decide
and
.Cm spawn .
.It Ev JUGGLER_RINGMASTER_BIN , Ev JUGGLER_TROUPE_BIN , Ev JUGGLER_SYSTEMD_RUN_BIN , Ev JUGGLER_MOXY_BIN
The binaries the substrate verbs execute.
Precedence: the
.Fl -ringmaster ,
.Fl -troupe ,
.Fl -systemd-run
or
.Fl -moxy
flag, then the variable, then the store path burned in at build time,
then the bare name on
.Ev PATH .
In the nix build ringmaster, troupe and systemd-run are burned in; moxy is
looked up on
.Ev PATH
unless the juggler was built by
.Cm mkJuggler
with a moxy, which burns that moxy in.
.It Ev JUGGLER_MOXY_URL
An already-running MCP upstream for
.Cm run
to use instead of launching moxy
.Pq tests .
.Cm spawn
passes it into the unit.
.It Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID
The caller's principal: the issuer for
.Cm spawn Fl -new-run ,
the run root for
.Cm spawn Fl -brief ,
the exiting principal for
.Cm exit-wake .
A unit gets its own, the child's.
.It Ev JUGGLER_OPERATOR_JID
The default of
.Cm spawn Fl -new-run Fl -operator-jid .
.It Ev TROUPE_MINT_PASSWORD_FILE , Ev TROUPE_MINT_USER
The spawner's minter credential, read by troupe from the environment
.Nm
passes it.
Required by
.Cm spawn Fl -new-run
and
.Cm spawn Fl -brief
.Pq the mints
and by
.Cm resolve
.Pq the account teardown; checked up front unless Fl -keep-accounts .
Stripped from every agent's unit, moxy and tool servers, and rejected in
a brief's
.Ql [env] .
.It Ev TROUPE_XMPP_*
The ambient XMPP identity that
.Cm decide
and the brief stanza post as.
Room administration, the canary post and the run input are made as the
run root instead; the host, port and minter variables
.Pq Ev TROUPE_XMPP_HOST , TROUPE_XMPP_PORT , TROUPE_MINT_*
are inherited by every troupe call.
.It Ev XDG_STATE_HOME
Root of juggler's state directory; see
.Sx FILES .
.It Ev SERVICE_RESULT , Ev EXIT_CODE , Ev EXIT_STATUS
Set by systemd for
.Cm exit-wake ;
see above.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "$XDG_STATE_HOME/juggler/runs/<run-key>/children/<digest>.brief.toml"
.It Pa ~/.local/state/juggler/control.sock
Juggler control socket.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/juggler/models/*.gguf
GGUF models visible to
.Cm models ,
.Cm start ,
and
.Cm download .
.It Pa ~/.local/share/juggler/models.toml
The remote-model registry.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/juggler/runs/<run-key>.json
A run's record: issuer, root principal and JID, credential reference,
room, root stanza, run job, holders, resolution.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/juggler/runs/<run-key>/ledger.json
The run ledger:
.Ql route ,
.Ql canary ,
.Ql subagent_stop
and
.Ql fallback
entries, closed by
.Cm resolve ,
then its
.Ql teardown
entries.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/juggler/runs/<run-key>/children/<digest>.json
A subagent's record; the digest is that of the template and task.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/juggler/runs/<run-key>/children/<digest>.brief.toml
The filled brief staged for the unit.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/juggler/runs/<run-key>/<principal>.pw
The troupe password of one identity minted for the run, mode 0600 in a
mode 0700 directory; deleted when
.Cm resolve
tears the account down.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/juggler/agents/<principal>/moxyfile
An agent's moxyfile, and the working directory of its moxy.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/juggler/exit-wakes/<job>
The sent-wake marker that keeps
.Cm exit-wake
idempotent.
.El
.Pp
.Ev XDG_STATE_HOME
defaults to
.Pa ~/.local/state .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
The RPC completed successfully (or the early-exit validation passed
for read-only subcommands).
.It 1
The RPC failed, an argument was missing or unrecognized, or the
control socket was unreachable.
.Nm
prints a one-line diagnostic to stderr before exiting.
.El
.Pp
The substrate verbs use 1 the same way and add their own meanings for
2 to 5, documented per verb above:
.Cm run
and
.Cm spawn Fl -wait
mirror the job state
.Pq 2 failed, 3 aborted, 4 interrupted ,
.Cm spawn Fl -wait
adds 5 for a cancelled job still running, and
.Cm decide
uses 4 for below threshold, 2 for no choice and 3 for a failed room
post.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start a coder model with the default alias, bound to localhost:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ juggler start qwen3-coder
juggler: started qwen3-coder at 127.0.0.1:43219 (pid 91234)
.Ed
.Pp
Start a second instance of the same model with a longer context window
and a distinguishing alias:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ juggler start qwen3-coder --alias coder-32k -- --ctx-size 32768
juggler: started coder-32k at 127.0.0.1:43221 (pid 91241)
.Ed
.Pp
List what's running:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ juggler list
ALIAS         MODEL         BIND       PORT   PID    UPTIME
coder-32k     qwen3-coder   127.0.0.1  43221  91241  12s
qwen3-coder   qwen3-coder   127.0.0.1  43219  91234  2m
.Ed
.Pp
Inspect a single instance with humanized uptime:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ juggler status qwen3-coder
alias:      qwen3-coder
model:      qwen3-coder
bind:       127.0.0.1
port:       43219
pid:        91234
started:    2026-05-19T12:00:00Z (2m0s ago)
.Ed
.Pp
Stop one:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ juggler stop coder-32k
juggler: stopped coder-32k
.Ed
.Pp
Register a process-less gateway endpoint and confirm it in the unified
registry:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ juggler model add openrouter-kimi --style openai-compat --url https://openrouter.ai/api/v1 --token "$OPENROUTER_API_KEY"
juggler: registered remote model "openrouter-kimi"
$ juggler model list
NAME               KIND    STYLE
qwen3-coder        local
openrouter-kimi    remote  openai-compat
.Ed
.Pp
Send a single prompt directly, bypassing clown and claude-code entirely:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ juggler prompt qwen3-coder "hello"
Hello! How can I help you today?
.Ed
