.Sh CAVEATS
The
.Cm download
subcommand never goes through the daemon.
This is intentional: juggler's
.Cm DownloadModel
RPC is synchronous, and the bubbletea progress UI lives in
.Nm
because the model registry and HTTP fetch are
.Xr jugglermodels 3
concerns that predate juggler.
Clown-side automation (planned in FDR-0011 / plan 2) does use the RPC
since clown is not terminal-attached.
.Pp
The
.Cm mcp
subcommand is likewise not meant for interactive human invocation: it
runs a long-lived stdio server that Claude Code spawns itself via the
.Cm clown-builtin-juggler
plugin's
.Sq stdioServers
entry, not something a person types at a shell prompt.
It deliberately ships no auto-allow hook, so every
.Sq juggler-prompt
call defers to Claude Code's native permission prompt; see
.Pa docs/plans/2026-07-11-juggler-subagent-tool-design.md
for the reasoning.
